<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!-- Allocator stress scene. Not a beauty shot: it exists so the shadow atlas
     carves itself up the way LIGHTING_PLAN.md 4.1 sketches, which the showcase
     cannot show.

     The showcase's lights all sit within ~15 units of the camera with radii over
     100, so every score (radius / distance) lands in the hundreds against a
     top-tier threshold of 0.50 — the tiering saturates and every light gets the
     largest tile it can have. Variable resolution goes untested.

     Here every light's intensity is *derived* from the score it is meant to
     have. scene.lightRadius inverts the shader falloff 1/(kConstant + d^2), so
     radius = sqrt(peak*255 - 1) with peak = max(colour) * diffuse * intensity;
     solving it the other way gives the intensity that puts a light at a chosen
     distance into a chosen tier. Rings at scores 0.75 / 0.30 / 0.13 therefore
     land in the 1024 / 512 / 256 tiers, and the point-light rings halve one step
     from there, which is how a 128 tile appears at all.

     64 lights, all of them casting: 41 coloured key lights in rings, then 23
     dim white fill lights, which is MaxLights exactly. Run it with:
         go run . -scene stress.xml
     and dump the partition with [debug] dumpAtlas = 5. -->
