	<!-- Dim white fill lights, added to push the atlas and the bake past what the
	     41 coloured lights above reach. Same derivation as the rest of the file,
	     with the one extra step a point light needs: solve the score backwards at
	     each light's own distance, radius = score * distance, then
	     intensity = 1000 * (radius^2 + 1) / 255 — the 1000 because toLight divides
	     a point light's intensity by it and the coloured rings above already carry
	     that factor.

	     They land between 13 and 112, the same band as the coloured far ring
	     (24-48) rather than the showcase's radii-over-100 key lights, so they read
	     as fill. The near ring sits close to the camera on purpose: score is
	     radius / distance, so proximity rather than brightness is what buys a
	     light a big tile, and that is the only way to fill the 256 pool without
	     making these bright.

	     Point lights rather than spots on purpose: six faces each, so 23 lights
	     buy 138 tiles. That is the bake cost this scene exists to measure; spots
	     would have bought 23.

	     23 is not a round number, it is the whole remaining budget. MaxLights is
	     64 and the scene above is 41. The atlas has room for more and the uniform
	     block does not, which is LIGHTING_PLAN.md 4.5's "77 against 64" arriving
	     in practice. -->
